{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "upwind1_D_periodic_ast_fixture",
    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/upwind1_D_periodic: a minimal consuming model binding N=8 at the import edge. The plain match D(u,x) must lower, through the section-9.6.3 fixpoint, to the rule's makearray — interior [2,8] holding the backward-difference aggregate, the i=1 face holding the explicit periodic wrap (u[1]-u[8])/dx — with all metaparameters folded and the free name dx surviving in the expanded body (the grid's consumer-supplied geometry contract). The model fulfills that contract with x0 = 0 and dx = 1/8; the dx expression is spelled with the literal 8 because the edge binding closes N before it reaches this document's scope (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm). The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST across bindings.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "ast",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d",
      "rule:upwind1_D_periodic"
    ]
  },
